     "dump": "music",
     "doc": "music: the songs of the epoch (dbmusic rows). Without epochs.yaml the songs come from dbmusic's per-epoch\nflags (EEMusicObject::LoadTable fills this; the space age plays the nano age's songs, as the original did)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mHighTechTools",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": false,
     "dump": "high_tech_tools",
     "doc": "the citizen of the epoch: beams: the mining beam, the shot effect (EEUGGather, EEUnitClass)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mRemovalEffects",
     "type": "int_list",
     "dump": "removal_effects",
     "doc": "a unit removed by a research (EEPlayUnitEffect): effects and a sound at its place, a thunder every n-th unit: dbgfxeffects rows"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mRemovalSound",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 374,
     "dump": "removal_sound",
     "doc": "dbsounds row (Lightning)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mRemovalPitchOffset",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.0,
     "dump": "removal_pitch_offset",
     "doc": "added to the sound's pitch (not below -1)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mRemovalThunder",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 442,
     "dump": "removal_thunder",
     "doc": "dbsounds row (Thunder 2)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mRemovalThunderEvery",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 0,
     "dump": "removal_thunder_every",
     "doc": "a thunder when the unit id is a multiple of this (0: never)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "EEAIPersonalityRule",
   "rust": "AIPersonalityRule",
   "section": "aipersonalities.yaml",
   "doc": "A computer player's personality (docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.8): the tuning of its decisions that is not in dbcpbehavior.\nThe defaults are \"balanced\", the tuning the benchmarks of §8.10-8.11 settled on.",
   "fields": [
    {
     "cpp": "mID",
     "type": "string",
     "dump": "id"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mNextScript",
     "type": "string",
     "default": "test_opening",
     "dump": "next_script",
     "doc": "the next engine's strategy (docs/AI_LUA_PLAN.md §3): the Lua module a computer seat with the next engine runs,\nData/ai/<name, dots as folders>.lua; the classic engine ignores it. Until stage S3's boom script, the S1 test\nopening ported to Lua"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mEpochPressureStart",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.3,
     "dump": "epoch_pressure_start",
     "doc": "epoch pressure (the elapsed share of the epoch timer's span): a paid advance is asked for from mEpochPressureStart;\nits reserve grows from nothing there to the whole cost at mEpochPressureFull. Low: tall (tech); high: wide."
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mEpochPressureFull",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.8,
     "dump": "epoch_pressure_full"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mStoneSpan",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 30.0,
     "dump": "stone_span",
     "doc": "the Prehistoric's pressure instead: the game time over this many minutes, so the Stone Age is asked for and\nreserved on that schedule (docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.27; 30: the Stone Age at about 25 minutes); 0: the epoch timer"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mSafeBonus",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.25,
     "dump": "safe_bonus",
     "doc": "from the Stone Age, while no stronger enemy army is near the town, the epoch pressure is this much higher: the\nadvance is asked for sooner and its reserve fills faster; a threat drops it back (docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.29)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mSurplus",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 1000,
     "dump": "surplus",
     "doc": "the economy (EECPResourceManager): the gatherer split's stock correction, the citizen target, rebalancing:\na resource with more in stock ..."
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mSurplusCut",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.5,
     "dump": "surplus_cut",
     "doc": "... gets this share of its gatherers"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mLowStock",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 150,
     "dump": "low_stock",
     "doc": "a resource with less in stock ..."
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mFloor",
     "type": "float_array",
     "default": [
      0.1,
      0.25,
      0.05,
      0.05,
      0.05
     ],
     "dump": "floor",
     "doc": "... at least this share (food, wood, stone, gold, iron)",
     "count": 5
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mMaxCitizenShare",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.7,
     "dump": "max_citizen_share",
     "doc": "the citizen target is at most this share of the pop cap"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mWoodSlots",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 15,
     "dump": "wood_slots",
     "doc": "wood's gatherer capacity (trees are not resource-center units)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mMovesPerCycle",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 3,
     "dump": "moves_per_cycle",
     "doc": "busy gatherers moved to a short resource per 10 s"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mDemandSplit",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "demand_split",
     "doc": "the gatherer split: by the tiered demand less the stock (EECPResourceManager.cpp EECPRMSplitByDemand; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md\n§8.21), or false: the original's needs ledger with the stock correction above"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mCoastFishing",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "coast_fishing",
     "doc": "fishing off any coast from the Stone Age (EECPResourceManager.cpp EECPRMCoastBoatsWanted; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md\n§8.26): a dock, up to 8 boats, at most 2 docks from the build lists; the original fished only on island maps"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mForagePatches",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "forage_patches",
     "doc": "forage patches (docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.27): about mining_limit gatherers a patch (the food capacity no longer\ncounts the bush gatherers), a settlement on a patch with no drop site within 4 tiles, hunting slots by the game\nnear home, 3 patches kept claimed in the Prehistoric and 5 later, up to 16 fishing boats"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mClaimNeeded",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "claim_needed",
     "doc": "a centre claimed for the next epoch's missing stone, gold or iron, and no epoch reserve while an advance cannot\nbe reached (docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.27)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mEarlyTownCenters",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 2,
     "dump": "early_town_centers",
     "doc": "before the Bronze Age a settlement becomes a town centre only while the player has fewer than this many, and no\ntown centre becomes a capitol (the owner: \"upgrading a settlement to a capitol early game is mostly a waste of\nfood\"; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.29); 0: the original's timers"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mEarlyTrainers",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 2,
     "dump": "early_trainers",
     "doc": "before the Copper Age at most this many barracks and this many archery ranges (dbcpbehavior asks for 7 and 6;\nthe owner: \"no more than 2 barracks and 2 archery ranges pre-copper\"); 0: no cap"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mPatchExpand",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "patch_expand",
     "doc": "before the Copper Age (no farms yet) the claim range grows when no forage patch is left in it (a playtest AI had\nno food gatherer for 45 minutes and 1399 of the Copper Age's 1584 food; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.29)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mStandingArmy",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.25,
     "dump": "standing_army",
     "doc": "military pressure: the standing army the player keeps, per worker (citizens and fishing boats); up to the\noriginal's military share of the pop cap"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mArmyFloor",
     "type": "float",
     "default": 0.1,
     "dump": "army_floor",
     "doc": "while the standing army is short of its target, the floor share of the gatherers on what its unit costs rises by\nup to this much (by the shortfall, split by the unit's cost): more army, less economy"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mMilitia",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "militia",
     "doc": "the town's answer to an attack group on its citizens (EECPResourceManager.cpp EECPRMMilitia; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md\n§8.25): the nearby soldiers and as many of the nearest citizens as the odds need fight, or the citizens run"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mMilitiaTowers",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "militia_towers",
     "doc": "the militia counts the built towers near the attack, and citizens that cannot fight run to the nearest tower\n(docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.26)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mPrehistoricArmy",
     "type": "int",
     "default": 4,
     "dump": "prehistoric_army",
     "doc": "the Prehistoric army is a mobile defence force of at most this many soldiers, unless enemy soldiers near the town\nare stronger than it (EEComputerPlayer.cpp CanAfford; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.26); 0: no cap (the rush)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mPrehistoricAttacks",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": false,
     "dump": "prehistoric_attacks",
     "doc": "attack groups against an enemy in the Prehistoric (false: none, the defence still forms; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.27)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mStoneAttacks",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": false,
     "dump": "stone_attacks",
     "doc": "attack groups against an enemy in the Stone Age (false: none, the defence still forms; docs/AI_RESEARCH.md §8.29)"
    },
    {
     "cpp": "mNavalFlee",
     "type": "bool",
     "default": true,
     "dump": "naval_flee",
     "doc": "units hit by a warship they cannot answer leave (boats to the farthest dock, citizens and melee inland)"
    }
   ]
  },
